    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in SSc:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " tocilizumab (anti-IL-6) preserves lung function in SSc-ILD; becoming an alt to mycophenolate, esp w predominant polyarthritis; rituximab is being evaluated for CTD-ILD and may have efficacy; skin: tocilizumab and rituximab (among others) have shown modest benefit."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) dose, systemic sclerosis-associated interstitial lung disease (SSc-ILD):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " SSc-ILD: 162 mg once weekly SC."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ↑ risk of serious infections that may lead to hospitalization or death; most pts were taking concomitant immunosuppressants such as methotrexate or corticosteroids. Test for latent TB b4 ACTEMRA use and during therapy (except pts w COVID-19); start treatment for latent infection prior to ACTEMRA use."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " known hypersensitivity to ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) GI perforation:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " GI perforation reported, primarily as complications of diverticulitis; use w caution in pts who may be at ↑ risk; promptly evaluate fever, new onset abdominal Sx, and a change in bowel habits for early identification."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) hepatotoxicity:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Obtain liver test panel (ALT, AST, alkaline phosphatase, total bilirubin) b4 ACTEMRA and every 4 to 8 wks for the first 6 mo, then every 3 mo; ⍉ initiate in RA, GCA or SSc-ILD pts w ALT or AST > 1.5× ULN; discontinue if ALT or AST > 5× ULN."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) lab monitoring:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ initiate in RA, GCA and SSc-ILD pts w ANC less than 2000 per mm3; if ANC less than 500 per mm3 treatment is not recommended. ⍉ initiate in RA, GCA and SSc-ILD pts w platelets below 100,000 per mm3; if platelets less than 50,000 per mm3 treatment is not recommended. Assess lipid parameters approximately 4 to 8 wks following initiation of ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) live vaccines:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ use of live vaccines concurrently w ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) CYP450 interaction:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Inhibition of IL-6 signaling in RA pts treated w tocilizumab may restore CYP450 activities to higher levels than in the absence of tocilizumab, leading to ↑ metabolism of CYP450 substrate drugs. On initiation or discontinuation of ACTEMRA, perform therapeutic monitoring of effect (e.g., warfarin) or drug concentration (e.g., cyclosporine or theophylline) and adjust the dose as needed."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV boxed warning — infusion reactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Fatal infusion-related reactions w/in 24 h of RITUXAN infusion; approximately 80% of fatal reactions occurred w first infusion; monitor pts and discontinue RITUXAN infusion for severe reactions."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV boxed warning — mucocutaneous reactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Severe mucocutaneous reactions, some w fatal outcomes."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV boxed warning — HBV reactivation:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " HBV reactivation, in some cases resulting in fulminant hepatitis, hepatic failure, and death. Screen all pts for HBV infection b4 treatment initiation and monitor pts during and after treatment; discontinue RITUXAN and concomitant medications in the event of HBV reactivation."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV boxed warning — PML:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML) resulting in death."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV infections:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Serious, incl fatal, bacterial, fungal, and new or reactivated viral infections can occur during and following the completion of RITUXAN-based therapy. Discontinue RITUXAN for serious infections and institute appropriate anti-infective therapy."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV cardiac reactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Cardiac adverse reactions incl ventricular fibrillation, myocardial infarction, and cardiogenic shock may occur; discontinue infusions for serious or life-threatening cardiac arrhythmias; perform cardiac monitoring during and after all infusions in pts who develop clinically significant arrhythmias or who have a Hx of arrhythmia or angina."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV live vaccines:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Vaccination w live virus vaccines is not recommended b4 or during treatment; administer non live vaccines at least 4 wks prior to a course of RITUXAN."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
